{
  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a sustained downtrend (e.g., falling from ~72 to ~61) with neutral sentiment, the model's upward forecast is systematically biased; apply a downward correction of 5-8% to counteract mean reversion pressure.",
    "If sentiment turns positive (0.20+) while price is at a local low or flat, the model often underestimates volatility and fails to capture subsequent sharp spikes; increase forecast variance by 10-15%.",
    "In volatile regimes with mixed sentiment (positive/negative swings), the model exhibits significant lag in reacting to sudden reversals; reduce forecasted growth rates by 20-30% to account for delayed momentum shifts.",
    "When price history shows high-frequency oscillation within a narrow band, the model's linear extrapolation leads to overshooting; apply a dampening factor of 0.85 to the projected trajectory.",
    "If sentiment is consistently neutral (0.00) during a period of structural price decline, assume the market is absorbing bad news without immediate reaction; do not trust the model's recovery signals until sentiment shifts or volatility increases."
  ]
}
